112
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:53,311
They may be living on the rez.
他们可能住在雷兹。

113
00:14:53,311 --> 00:15:00,180
They may be watching from Española, Las Cruces, Belen, Hobbs, or even Gallup.
他们可能在埃斯帕诺拉、拉斯克鲁塞斯、贝伦、霍布斯甚至盖洛普观看。

114
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:04,960
Some of them may be growing up in households where money is tight,
他们中的一些人可能在资金紧张的家庭中长大，

115
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:13,860
Where their parents work more than one job, or where they wonder what opportunities will actually be available to them when they grow up.
他们的父母从事不止一份工作，或者他们想知道自己长大后实际上可以获得哪些机会。

116
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:25,200
I want every child watching to know that your dreams matter, and that New Mexico is a place where you can build the life You want.
我希望每一个观看的孩子都知道你的梦想很重要，新墨西哥州是一个你可以创造生活的地方你想要。

117
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:34,970
Where you can build the life you want close to the communities that raised you.
在这里，您可以在靠近养育您的社区的地方过上您想要的生活。

118
00:15:35,690 --> 00:15:40,510
Here in New Mexico, we can do anything.
在新墨西哥州，我们可以做任何事情。

119
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:47,460
And I know this because I am living proof.
我知道这一点，因为我就是活生生的证据。

120
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:55,090
I spent years working on my sobriety.
我花了很多年的时间努力保持清醒。

121
00:15:56,010 --> 00:16:02,030
I raised a child in poverty as a single mom, registered voters in a res car,
我作为一个单亲妈妈在贫困中养育了一个孩子，在一辆救援车里登记选民，

122
00:16:02,115 --> 00:16:11,070
Along dirt roads, and in dust storms, to eventually serve in the halls of Congress and become the first Native American to serve as
沿着土路，在沙尘暴中，最终在国会大厅任职，并成为第一个担任国会议员的美国原住民

123
00:16:11,070 --> 00:16:12,750
A US cabinet secretary.
美国内阁秘书。

124
00:16:12,965 --> 00:16:22,580
And now I'm heading to the Roundhouse to serve as your next governor.
现在我要去圆屋担任你们的下一任州长。

125
00:16:31,296 --> 00:16:43,990
As I've said, as I've said, my journey has never been mine alone.
正如我说过的，正如我说过的，我的旅程从来都不是我一个人的。

126
00:16:44,890 --> 00:16:49,630
My parents raised me to work hard and to care, and I thank them both.
我的父母养育了我努力工作和关心他人，我感谢他们俩。

127
00:16:50,522 --> 00:16:59,670
To Soma, my sisters and my brother, my wonderful extended family and former colleagues,
致索玛、我的姐妹和兄弟、我美好的大家庭和前同事，

128
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:05,410
I see the sacrifices you all have made for your families and our communities,
我看到你们为家人和社区做出的牺牲，

129
00:17:06,110 --> 00:17:07,370
And I am forever grateful.
我永远心存感激。

130
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:13,030
I stand here tonight because of the many generations who came before me,
今晚我站在这里是因为在我之前的许多代人，

131
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:20,890
The family who looked out for me, and the New Mexicans who have always believed that a better New Mexico is possible.
照顾我的家人，以及始终相信更好的新墨西哥州是可能的新墨西哥人。

132
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:30,580
I will fight for that fair shot in a New Mexico that believes in all of us.
我将在相信我们所有人的新墨西哥州争取公平的机会。

133
00:17:31,322 --> 00:17:37,380
A New Mexico where anyone can grow up, build a family, find a good job,
一个任何人都可以成长、建立家庭、找到好工作的新墨西哥州，

134
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,720
And be proud to call this beautiful state home.
并自豪地称之为这个美丽的州府。

135
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:43,815
This is a responsibility.
这是一种责任。

136
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:47,320
This is the responsibility we all share.
这是我们大家共同的责任。

137
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:52,460
So tonight this campaign ends, and our real work begins.
今晚这个活动结束了，我们真正的工作开始了。

138
00:17:53,140 --> 00:18:01,200
We now turn our a thousands of conversations into action, our promises into progress,
我们现在将数千次对话转化为行动，将我们的承诺转化为进步，

139
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:06,700
And our shared vision into a better future for all New Mexicans.
我们共同的愿景是为所有新墨西哥人创造更美好的未来。

140
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:20,960
With our grit, our creativity, our determination, and our willingness to look out for each other,
凭借我们的勇气、我们的创造力、我们的决心以及我们互相照顾的意愿，

141
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:24,600
I know we can accomplish anything together.
我知道我们可以一起完成任何事情。

142
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:29,920
And that's why I know New Mexico's brightest days are ahead of us.
这就是为什么我知道新墨西哥州最光明的日子就在前方。

143
00:18:30,508 --> 00:18:35,120
God bless New Mexico.
上帝保佑新墨西哥州。

144
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,300
God bless our country.
上帝保佑我们的国家。

145
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,320
Thank you all so much.
非常感谢大家。

146
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:40,971
Thank you.
谢谢你。
